<?xml version="1.0"?>
<ScenContainer xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance" xmlns:xsd="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema">
  <ScenTitle>BALTAP - Repräsentative Schnellbootlage - 10 Years Later, 1980</ScenTitle>
  <ScenDescription>&lt;BODY scroll=auto&gt;&lt;P&gt;In 1967 the Federal German Navy played a wargame to evaluate the cost-value ratio of the planned modernisation of "Zobel Class" (Type 142) FPB's to "Type 142A" (upgrade with M-20 fire-control radar and DM2A1 wire-guided torpedos). This study&amp;nbsp;also showed how the&amp;nbsp;operational situation&amp;nbsp;of FPB's in the Baltic&amp;nbsp;was assesed by the experts of the Navy.&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;This scenario plays 10 years later in February 1980 with FPB's which were in service then:&lt;BR&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp; * Type 142A Zobel Class: equipped with wire-guided torpedoes&lt;BR&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp; * Type 148 Tiger Class: equipped with MM38 ASM&lt;BR&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp; * Type 143 Albatros Class: equipped with MM38 ASM and wire-guided torpedoes&lt;BR&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp; * Osa II&amp;nbsp;Class: equipped with&amp;nbsp;SS-N-2b&lt;BR&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp; * Tarantul II Class: equipped with SS-N-2c&lt;BR&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp; * Nanuchka I Class: equipped with&amp;nbsp;SS-N-9&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;&lt;FONT color=#0080ff&gt;**********************************&lt;BR&gt;In the night 8&amp;nbsp;German FPB's should attack an&amp;nbsp;OPFOR supply convoy underway to&amp;nbsp;replenish a beachhead on Zealand.&lt;BR&gt;OPFOR has 3 Fitter-missions available for armed recon. Federal German Navy has 2 F-104-missions available for armed recon.&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;&lt;FONT color=#0080ff&gt;The OPFOR convoy consits of 4 Alligator LST's&amp;nbsp;escorted by&amp;nbsp;a Krivak I&amp;nbsp;Class&amp;nbsp;FFG and a conventionally armed "Kotlin Mod. Class" destroyer.&amp;nbsp;A group of 3 "Osa II&amp;nbsp;Class"&amp;nbsp;missile boats, a group of 3 "Tarantul II&amp;nbsp;Class" missile boats&amp;nbsp;and a group of 3 "Nanuchka I Class" missile boats are escorting the convoy 10-15 miles in front of the HVU's.&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;&lt;FONT color=#0080ff&gt;No mines and no submarines in the operation area.&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;&lt;FONT color=#0080ff&gt;The German Units should attack the LST's as primary targets. Engagement of the&amp;nbsp;escorting missile boats&amp;nbsp;only in situations were this is absolutely necessary for fulfilling the mission.&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;&lt;FONT color=#0080ff&gt;The German&amp;nbsp;squadron&amp;nbsp;is splitted in 2 divisions and cruising&amp;nbsp;from the&amp;nbsp;southern exit of the "Great Belt" to "Moens Klint" (SOA 15-20 kn).&amp;nbsp;In vicinity of "Groensund" they split in 3 subdivisions and will attack the OPFOR convoy with&amp;nbsp;full speed. Emissions are allowed only occasionally by the leader boat.&lt;BR&gt;**********************************&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;&lt;FONT color=blue&gt;&lt;FONT color=#0080ff&gt;With a random generator, the boat types are automatically&amp;nbsp;selected on scenario start (4 options: all 8 boats of Type 142A; all Type 143; all Type 148; mixed Type 142A/143/148).&lt;BR&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/BODY&gt;</ScenDescription>
